            <ArticleTitle>[How participation in a clinical trial affects doctors' choice of treatment].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3987-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a retrospective cohort study, the effects of participation in a company-sponsored clinical trial on asthma drug prescribing were investigated. Ten trial-conducting practices were compared with 165 control practices. Conducting the trial did not influence guideline adherence measured as the prevalence of inhaled corticosteroid use among users of inhaled beta2-agonists. However, participation in the trial led to an increased preference for sponsor's drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
